    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d939">

                <pb facs="0801" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg791"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Stuart, J. Leighton: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-18T16:00:00+08:00">July 18, 1949—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 18—5:16 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1547. No reply from Peiping authorities and I am again forced to change my ETD. I
                    will not depart morning of 19th (Embtel 1537, <pb facs="0802" n="792"
                        xml:id="pg792"/> July 16 to Department, repeated Canton 645, Taipei 64) as
                    planned and will inform you promptly of new ETD as soon as decision reached on
                    our exit permits.</p>
                <p>Sent Department; repeated OffEmb Canton 648, Taipei 65.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
